From fe5b9e69ed36825d153f4fb718eccd5bd2905fa6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 03:07:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(readme): this is the prx receiver, not the bounded.tools
 website

Checkouts of bounded-systems/site commonly live in a directory named
bounded.tools/ (its old README said to clone that URL), so this repo gets
mistaken for the website and vice versa. State up front which repo this
is, cite bounded-systems/site by URL, and point at the issue that tracks
the naming.

Refs bounded-systems/site#32

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CVjvRP7P9oSiX3uhjK1xsz
---
 README.md | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index e586891..5d8a8d3 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -6,6 +6,15 @@ GitHub App [`bounded-systems-prx`](https://github.com/organizations/bounded-syst
 [app definition](https://github.com/bounded-systems/prx/blob/main/docs/github-app.md)
 (`.github/prx-app.manifest.json`), this repo owns the runtime.
 
+> **Not the website.** This repo is `bounded-systems/bounded.tools`, the
+> receiver Worker at `hooks.bounded.tools`. The website at <https://bounded.tools>
+> is a separate repo, [`bounded-systems/site`](https://github.com/bounded-systems/site)
+> (deployed as `bounded-tools-site`). Its old README said to clone
+> `bounded.tools.git`, so a local directory named `bounded.tools/` is often a
+> checkout of `site` — check `git remote get-url origin` before trusting the
+> directory name. Background and the rename proposal (not executed):
+> [bounded-systems/site#32](https://github.com/bounded-systems/site/issues/32).
+
 > **Status: DEPLOYED, not yet ingesting.** First light 2026-08-15 (run
 > 31889379320): `GET https://hooks.bounded.tools/health` returns `ok` and
 > `/ci.json` serves a valid snapshot. The receiver still **rejects every
